WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.140
Before we get into the course objectives,
I want to take you through two tools you will

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.760
need to install so that you can follow along
with what you see in this course.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.450
The downloads and installations are pretty
straightforward, but know that what you will

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.550
see on the websites I am about to show you
now may differ from what you will end up seeing,

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.110
as these tools get updated fairly frequently.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.190
First, you will need the Python engine.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:29.670
While it does come with some development tools,
the best way to ensure you have the engine

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.500
is to download it straight from the source,
python.org.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:41.039
I am on the site now and will select the latest
version of Python to download.

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:45.720
Your operating system will dictate which version
you download, but I downloaded and installed

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.860
the Windows Installer 64-bit version as I
am running Windows 11.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:56.570
Once that installation is complete, you will
need an Integrated Development Environment

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.469
app, which is a tool that supports one or
multiple programming languages.

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:07.840
PyCharm is a leading Python IDE, but I will
use Visual Studio code for this course, which

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.990
can be downloaded here.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:14.960
I use this tool because it supports all the
programming and markup languages covered in

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:23.030
the IT Specialist programming certification
courses, such as this course, HTML, CSS, JavaScript,

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:28.479
Java, and C#, for software development fundamentals.

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:33.110
You can take the default installation once
you have installed the Python engine.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.110
How do you know Python is installed correctly?

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.000
I’m glad you asked.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.460
To verify that Python is installed, open a
command prompt, as I am doing here, and then

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:49.190
type py and select the Enter key on the keyboard.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:55.869
If you see three arrows and some Python information,
Python is installed and ready to be used.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:02:01.580
Holding down the Ctrl key, selecting Z, and
then selecting the Enter key on the keyboard

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.980
closes the Python session within the command
prompt.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.319
Here is what Visual Studio Code looks like
once it is installed.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:16.330
The next step is installing the Python extension,
making writing, editing, and running Python

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.800
code easier.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:24.319
I will select the gear icon in the lower-left
corner of the screen, select Extensions, and

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:29.170
search for Python.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:34.740
I already have the extension installed, but
if you don’t, select Install to install

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.129
the extension and then restart Visual Studio
Code if necessary.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.480
One of the main benefits of the extension
is Intellisense, which helps us to write code

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:49.569
but also provides useful visual indicators
for any code that might contain syntax errors

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.739
and, thus, will not run correctly.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:59.330
As we go through each domain, a student folder
with practice files for each domain is accessible.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:08.540
To open a folder for a domain, we just need
to select File, Open Folder, select the folder

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:15.330
we want to open, and then choose Select Folder
to open that folder, as I am doing with the

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.349
Domain 1 student files.

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:22.910
Once you have completed these installations,
you can start learning and building with Python.

